    'sv-placed uses ORACLE placement (whole-session knowledge of which files are edited) — an upper bound; a deterministic online policy (start volatile, promote-on-proven-stability, demote-on-edit) would approach but not equal it.',
    'An edit provides no post-edit full content, so a single-version file block is version-bumped with a marker (size ~unchanged); reads carry real content. This under-models edit-driven size growth, not the cache dynamics.',
    'Non-file tool outputs (Bash/Grep) are kept identically in all arms (not deduped).',
